  "worked_solution": "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=-\\frac{k}{5}$ and $n=8$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-\\frac{k}{5})}^{8} & =1+8\\cdot (-\\frac{k}{5})+\\frac{8(8-1)}{2!}\\cdot {(-\\frac{k}{5})}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8k}{5}+\\frac{8\\cdot 7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{k}^{2}}{25}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8k}{5}+28\\cdot \\frac{{k}^{2}}{25}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-\\frac{8}{5}k+\\frac{28}{25}{k}^{2}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
